  <h1>Melody Loops</h1>
  <p>Improvise melodies over a chord progression</p>
</div>
<main>
<p>The Melody Loops page gives you chord-tone pads to improvise over — tap in time with a chord progression and every pad stays musically in key.</p>

<h2>Melody Pads</h2>
<p>The pad grid always plays notes belonging to the current chord, so anything you tap fits. Choose 8 or 12 pads for a wider range.</p>

<h2>Pad Octave &amp; Loop Octave</h2>
<ul class="guide">
  <li><strong>Pad Oct</strong> — shifts the melody pads up or down an octave, instantly, mid-performance</li>
  <li><strong>Loop Oct</strong> — separately shifts the octave of whatever's currently recorded in the loop, without touching what the pads themselves play</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Keeping these independent means you can record a bass-register loop, then shift the live pads up an octave to play a lead over it — without re-recording anything.</p></div>

<h2>Chord Pattern</h2>
<p>Choose a built-in progression to play underneath your melody — Pop/Rock, Blues, Jazz, Gospel, Soul/R&amp;B and more, in both major and minor. The chords advance automatically in time; your melody pads follow whatever chord is currently playing.</p>

<h2>Arp</h2>
<p>Toggles an arpeggiator on the chord accompaniment — instead of the chord playing as a block, its notes ripple in sequence underneath your melody.</p>

<h2>Key</h2>
<p>Tap Key Up to shift everything up 3 semitones. If a loop is playing, the change waits cleanly until the loop finishes before switching — never mid-bar.</p>

<h2>Loop Recorder</h2>
<p>Four independent loop slots let you record melody pad performances and play them back on a seamless cycle.</p>
<ul class="guide">
  <li>Tap an empty slot to arm it — recording starts cleanly on the next bar</li>
  <li>Tap while recording to stop early, or let it fill the full cycle automatically</li>
  <li>Tap a stopped slot to queue playback — it joins in cleanly on the next bar</li>
  <li>Tap a playing slot to queue a stop — it finishes the current loop first, never cuts off mid-phrase</li>
  <li>Hold a stopped slot for Re-record or Clear</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Loops recorded here have nothing to do with Sample Pads' own loop recorder — the two are entirely separate, so building a melody loop never affects anything you've built on the Samples page.</p></div>

<h2>Tone</h2>
<p>Tap the wave icon in the header to shape the sound of the melody pads themselves — nine instrument presets (Piano, E.Piano, Cosmic, Synth, Organ, Flute, Sax, Harpsi, Bell) plus full manual control over wave shape, detune, modulation, vibrato, attack, decay, sustain, filter resonance and stereo width.</p>

